+/// that object's record, resolve its chunk map, or read it under an `inode:<id>` key — so its
+/// reading has a hole in it. No obligation is drained on what such a reading did NOT find, and the
+/// pass certifies nothing until the record is repaired. Named as GC names one.
+fn emit_unaccounted(action: &'static str, object: &str, fault: &dyn Display) {
