+//! Issue #681 (slice 4b of 7 of the #635 re-slicing, proposal 0016 decision 7(e)): **the three
+//! maintenance passes that walk the committed namespace themselves — reconstruction, backfill,
+//! rebalance — resolve every committed object the way every other consumer resolves one, contain
+//! per object what they cannot read, and refuse (rather than abort or silently discard) the work
+//! this slice does not own.**
+//!
+//! On the base all three read the chunk map inline out of the inode record
+//! (`record.chunk_map.as_flat().ok_or(SegmentedMapUnsupported)?`, seven sites), so ONE segmented
+//! object turns repair, fill and drain into an `Err` for EVERY object in the store — and these are
+//! the passes that *restore redundancy*. An undecodable record ends the walk the same way.
+//!
+//! Six legs, each driving ALL THREE passes over ONE store — one test per property, never one per
+//! pass. The pinned decisions ride as sub-assertions: leg 3 carries the empty-queue and raw-key
+//! decisions, leg 2 "one refusal line per object", leg 6 "attribution before the work".
+//!
+//! **No assertion here names the answer's new shape** — the production files are reverted under the
+//! per-fix red leg, so a symbol this patch introduces would make that leg fail to COMPILE and the
+//! red would degrade to "a symbol is missing". `Reconciled::Blocked` is base-visible.
+
+#![forbid(unsafe_code)]
+
